    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d444">

                <pb facs="0615" n="329" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg329"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/1861a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        British Ambassador</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Spring Rice</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-01-05">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 5, 1916</hi>
                        </date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Ambassador</hi>: As
                    the Department has received no reply from your Government to its note of October
                        21<anchor n="2" xml:id="d444-f1"/> in regard to British measures believed by
                    this Government to restrict its legitimate trade with belligerent and neutral
                    countries of Europe, I have to ask whether you will be kind enough to inquire of
                    your Government when we may expect to receive its formal answer. As you know,
                    the matter will probably come up for discussion in the Congress and I hope the
                    reply of your Government, acceding to our contentions which seemed to me
                    perfectly well founded, will shortly be received in order that the situation may
                    be speedily relieved.</p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
